# Implementation - Movie Recommendation API

## Implementation Plan

The development of the Movie Recommendation API follows a structured approach starting with requirement analysis where the core functionality of movie data delivery and user authentication is defined. The backend architecture is then designed using Express.js to handle routing, middleware, and API responses efficiently. Each module including authentication, movie routes, and carousel data is implemented separately following modular design principles. The database schema using PostgreSQL is set up to store user data and movie information. API endpoints are created to serve data from JSON files in the CustomData directory. Authentication is integrated using Passport.js with Google OAuth strategy. Finally, Swagger documentation is configured to provide API reference for developers.

## Standards Used

The implementation follows RESTful API standards ensuring proper HTTP methods are used for each operation. The JSON data format is used consistently for all API responses with success and error states. Express.js conventions are followed for middleware placement, route definitions, and error handling. Passport.js is implemented according to OAuth 2.0 standards for authentication. The project structure follows Node.js best practices with separate routes, middleware, and configuration directories. Environment variables are used for sensitive configuration following the twelve-factor app methodology. CORS is configured to allow specific origins for security. API versioning is prepared through URL structure for future scalability.

